@startuml sd07_maintenance_switch
!include ../style.iuml
title SD-07 Maintenance switch command from the CTC Office (UC-09, UC-11)
autonumber

actor Dispatcher as D
participant "CTC Office" as CTC
participant "Central Harness" as H
participant "Track Ctrl HW\n(host + Pi)" as TC
participant "Wayside" as W
participant "PLC (user program\n+ vital block)" as PLC
participant "Track Model" as TM

D -> CTC : maintenance mode: set switch Red:15 to reverse
CTC -> H : outputs: switch command (Red, 15, reverse)
H -> TC : step: ctc.switch_commands = {Red:15: reverse}
TC -> W : scan(...)
W -> W : CTCSW_15 = 1, CTCREV_15 = 1
W -> PLC : scan both channels
alt blocks at the switch occupied (LOCK_15)
  PLC --> W : SW_15 = SWREV_15 (locked where it reports)
  note right of W : the command waits until the train has passed
else clear
  PLC --> W : SW_15 = 1 (the program obeys the CTC Office)
end
W --> TC : switch_commands[Red 15] = reverse;\nswitch_requests shown as "CTC asks" in the window
TC --> H : outputs
H -> TM : switch command reverse
TM -> TM : switch machine moves
TM -> H : (next tick) switch_positions[Red 15] = reverse
H -> TC : step: track_model.switch_positions
TC --> H : CtcReport: block 15 switch_position = reverse
H -> CTC : switch state
CTC --> D : map shows switch 15 reversed
note over CTC, W
  While SW_15 and SWREV_15 differ (moving or failed), the program
  turns signal 15 red and zeroes authority over the switch.
end note
D -> CTC : leave maintenance mode
CTC -> H : no switch commands
H -> TC : step: ctc.switch_commands = {}
TC -> W : CTCSW_15 = 0: the program routes the switch again
@enduml
